                Elections in modern democracies are no longer won solely on physical rally grounds and loudspeaker announcements. Today, over 75% of registered voters—particularly youth, women, and undecided swing demographics—form their political perceptions through smartphone screens, viral WhatsApp forwarded videos, YouTube commentaries, and Instagram Reels. In a high-stakes campaign, how effectively a candidate communicates their development vision and responds to opposition attacks online directly determines polling booth outcomes.
              </p>
              <p>
